From 96afea412eb6aa5f6c1559b39123c29dabab1bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:39:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(ui): the shared report scrubs every path, on every
 system

The Report door's text leaves the machine. The first form replaced only
the project's own path in the status line; other status texts (for
example `open failed: <path>`) sent a full directory path. The shared
report now passes its whole text through report_scrub::scrub_paths:
each path-like word (Windows drive and UNC, POSIX, `~`, relative forms,
either separator, folder names with spaces) shrinks to its last
component. The status strip and the in-app Debug info do not change.

file_name_only now reads `/` and `\` on every system, so a Windows
machine-file path in a project opened on Linux or macOS gives its file
name too (Path::file_name sees no separator there).

Refs #2744

